            "snippets": [
              "# The U.S.-China Trade War: Different Messages\nSecond, even if this leads to escalation, the United States has less to lose since its exports to China are $130 billion while China's exports to the United States are $505 billion a year. In a tit-for-tat exercise, it is argued, China will run out of exports to levy retaliatory tariffs upon long before the United States does",

